---
/**
 * website/src/pages/caps-and-costs.astro — the caps-and-costs guide (website plan, Task
 * W1.5).
 *
 * The page is a heading and the guide itself: what a cap is and how to set it, and what
 * runs actually cost are `src/components/CapsCosts.astro`, which renders the CLI's own
 * reference and the owner-run aggregation's own output. Nothing is written here, and
 * nothing on this page is a figure the aggregation did not produce (F26, F31, F33, D96,
 * D97).
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import CapsCosts from '../components/CapsCosts.astro'
---

<Base title="Caps and costs">
  <h1>Caps and costs</h1>

  <p>
    Fugaro bounds what a run may spend, and it records what its runs actually spent. This page
    is the caps that bound it, the commands that set them, and the measurements themselves —
    each rendered from the repository's own output rather than described here.
  </p>

  <CapsCosts />
</Base>
